  "summary": "DOAC dose review for the week of 10/19/2026 under RBC-PHARM-07. All 9 patients were reviewed. 8 doses were changed and 1 was already correct. Each change has a signed progress note citing the results, orders and letters it relied on.\n\nApixaban:\n- Dorothy Ashworth (pt-0040): 5 mg → 2.5 mg twice daily. She is 83, and her creatinine at St. Brigid on 10/15 was 150 µmol/L, which is 1.70 mg/dL. That is two criteria. New order mr-t0001, note doc-t0002.\n- Walter Kowalczyk (pt-0001): 5 mg → 2.5 mg twice daily. He is 84 and weighed 57.6 kg on 10/14. That is two criteria. New order mr-t0009, note doc-t0010.\n- Raymond Duquette (pt-0041): 5 mg → 2.5 mg twice daily. He meets no criteria, but he has an active itraconazole order (mr-00359). Itraconazole was not changed. New order mr-t0007, note doc-t0008.\n- Gregory Lindahl (pt-0045): 5 mg → 2.5 mg twice daily. He meets no criteria, but a 9/18 St. Brigid infectious disease letter lists ritonavir 100 mg daily as a booster for darunavir. His HIV medicines were not changed. That letter asks to be consulted before new medicines start. No message has been sent to the ID clinic, so you may want to tell them about the apixaban. New order mr-t0011, note doc-t0012.\n- Harold Vance (pt-0002): 2.5 mg → 5 mg twice daily. The lower dose was set at his February kidney-injury discharge. Now only his age (82) counts: he weighed 143 lb (64.9 kg) on 10/20, and his creatinine that day was 1.21 mg/dL. New order mr-t0015, note doc-t0016.\n\nRivaroxaban (kidney function estimated with the Cockcroft-Gault formula):\n- Clarence Bauer (pt-0039): 20 mg → 15 mg daily. His clearance is 44 mL/min, using the 59 kg measured on 10/14. The 168 lb on 10/21 was a phone report, not a measured weight, so it was not used. New order mr-t0003, note doc-t0004.\n- Frank Delgado (pt-0003): 20 mg → 15 mg daily. His clearance is 44 mL/min, using 90 kg and the St. Brigid creatinine of 160 µmol/L (1.81 mg/dL) on 10/19. New order mr-t0005, note doc-t0006.\n- Eugene Moravec (pt-0038): 15 mg → 20 mg daily. His clearance is 56 mL/min using his actual weight of 96 kg, as the policy requires. The May reduction used ideal body weight. New order mr-t0013, note doc-t0014.\n- Marjorie Pellegrino (pt-0043): stays on 20 mg daily. Her clearance is 59 mL/min (75-year-old woman, 71 kg, creatinine 0.92). I didn't write a note because the policy only asks for one when the dose changes.\n\nNo other medications were changed. No patient was on 2.5 mg twice daily together with one of the interacting drugs, so there were no combination warnings to send to prescribers.",
  "resumed": false,
